# M9's done-when on QEMU with the selftest kernel (user/root/src/net.rs
# and servers.rs; docs/design.md, "Network scenarios"): 100 UDP datagrams
# sent through QEMU's forwarded port all come back. Root starts watch,
# uart and console, attaches as client 1 and points its output at
# console, sets up PCI (ECAM through carved device frames, virtio-net-pci
# at 00:02.0, its regions and MSI-X checked, the MSI bound to NV and MSI-X
# entry 0 programmed, bus mastering on once the driver's frames are
# mapped, configuration space and the MSI-X table unmapped), starts net
# (130), with QEMU's 10.0.2.15/24 via 10.0.2.2, and virtio-net (140),
# each in a CSpace and VSpace of its own sharing only the frame queues'
# frame, prints the servers: line with the root CNode's slots in use, and
# reads a line as client 1. virtio-net sets up the device and signals
# net, which takes the link block, ARPs for the gateway and pings it
# (libslirp answers both, from 52:55:0a:00:02:02). Then xtask sends 100
# datagrams of 8 to 1,472 bytes through the forwarded port, at most 8 at
# a time, and checks each echo. Enter ends it: root asks both servers'
# Stats, prints them and requires (root::check::net) no bad queue entry
# or used element, no IP or UDP checksum error, no frame dropped for want
# of a buffer on either side, and at least 100 datagrams echoed; the
# expect pins exactly 100.
cmdline: test=net
exit: success
nic: virtio-net
expect: root: cmdline "test=net"
expect: pci: ecam 0xe0000000, segment 0, buses 0-255
expect: pci: virtio-net at 00:02.0
expect: servers: virtio-net (priority 140, MSI-X IRQ
expect: net (priority 130); root CNode
expect: virtio-net: up: MAC 52:54:00:12:34:56, features VERSION_1 MAC STATUS, link up, queues 64 and 64
expect: net: up: 10.0.2.15/24 via 10.0.2.2, MAC 52:54:00:12:34:56
expect: echo: listening on UDP port 7
expect: net: gateway 10.0.2.2 is at 52:55:0a:00:02:02
expect: net: ping 10.0.2.2: reply 1, 56 bytes
udp_echo: 100
send: \r                           # root's line: report and end
expect: virtio-net: stats:
expect: , 0 dropped for no buffer, 0 bad used elements,
expect: , 0 bad queue entries,
expect: net: stats:
expect: , 100 datagrams echoed,
expect: , 0 frames dropped, 0 bad entries,
expect: TEST PASS
expect: DEBUG HALT 0 from TCB
forbid: TEST FAIL
forbid: KERNEL PANIC
